  data: {
    LLM: "As forehand, evaluate the 4 face-up cards carefully before choosing your contract. With many high cards and a strong suit, choose Sang or a trump contract. With weak cards, choose Pass.\n\nContract sequencing: save your most flexible contract (Valfri) for last so you can adapt to your hand. Spader should be chosen when you naturally have good spades. Don't waste Valfri on spades if you haven't played Spader yet.\n\nIn Sang (no-trump, win tricks), count the cards: with 16 tricks, forehand needs 8 â€” exactly half. Lead your strong suits first to establish winners. In Pass (avoid tricks), avoid leading and duck with low cards. Discard strategy: when picking up the 4 face-up cards, discard to strengthen your chosen contract â€” void a suit for trump contracts, or shed high cards for Pass.",
